  "description": "Canfield Brothers Riot 29\nThe Bros. changed the industry’s perception of 29er handling in 2011 with the Yelli Screamy, the first 29er with sub-17-inch chainstays and a playful and nimble ride. Here we are in 2015, and the all-new Canfield Brothers Riot pushes the bar further than ever, boasting the most aggressive 29er geometry to hit a full-suspension trail bike to date. Coupling 140 millimeters (5.5 inches) of the revolutionary active and efficient patented Canfield Balance Formula travel with the slack-and-low geometry Canfield Brothers is known for, the Riot is the most fun full-suspension 29er to ever hit the trail, up or down. Radically short 414-millimeter (16.3-inch) chainstays will let you snap turns like no one with big wheels should, while the 66.5-degree head angle gives you confidence where it counts. This ain’t your dad’s 29er.",
